* t41evwake.a -- CONF68K test t41: a pulse wakes a process already waiting,* and the value it wakes with is the pulsed one.** Claim (DOCS/claims.md): Ev$Pulse sets the event variable to d2, "then, the* Ev$Signl search routine is executed and the original event value is* restored" (page 1-25), and Ev$Wait returns "d1.l = actual event value"* (page 1-22).** t40 checks what a pulse leaves behind.  This checks the half t40 cannot* reach: that the pulse is seen at all.  Its entire observable effect is on* processes ALREADY in the event queue, because the value it sets is put back* before the call returns -- so a single process can never catch one, no* matter how quickly it looks.  Two processes are the minimum, and the second* has to be blocked before the first acts.** THE ORDERING, AND WHY IT IS THE HARD PART** Every other two-process test here has the parent act BEFORE it forks, which* is race-free for the reason fork.i gives: a child cannot have started* earlier than the call that created it.  This one needs the opposite -- the* child blocked first, the parent acting second -- and nothing a process can* do observes another's impending sleep.** So it uses fork.i's ready marker, with the residual race stated there:* SCRATCH/ready says the child is ABOUT to call Ev$Wait, not that it has* blocked.  RELDELAY is fork.i's own figure for that gap, far larger than the* handful of instructions between the marker and the trap.  Note that this* test cannot use contend, which is built around releasing a record lock; it* uses the pieces underneath it instead.** WHAT THE CHILD REPORTS** The value Ev$Wait handed back, in fork.i's 1000 band.  7 is the pulsed* value and the event was created holding 0, so the number distinguishes* every outcome that matters: 7 means the pulse was seen; 0 could only mean* the wait returned without the pulse; anything in the 2000 band means the* child could not set up.  A pulse that woke nobody produces no number at all* -- the child stays blocked, the parent's DONEMAX runs out, and it is killed* and reported as HUNG (902), which is exactly what os9exec did before the* event queue existed.** wInc is 0 so the value the child sees is the pulsed value and nothing else.* With a non-zero wait auto-increment the search would apply it between the* wake and the restore, and the manual does not say which of the two the* woken process is supposed to observe.  That is a real open question, and* not one this test needs to answer to check the claim it is about.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1FEvent set $53EvLink set 0EvCreat set 2EvDelet set 3EvWait set 4EvPulse set 9*INITVAL set 0WAITINC set 0SIGINC set 1PULSVAL set 7EXPECT set 7* psect t41evwake,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,4096,startstart* Role first: ckrole reads d5 and a5, which are entry registers and are* undefined the moment anything else runs. bsr ckrole tst.w d0 bne.w child** ---- parent: create the event, fork, and pulse it once the child waits ---- lea rdymark(pc),a0 bsr rmmark lea dnmark(pc),a0 bsr rmmark* lea evname(pc),a0 move.l #INITVAL,d0 move.w #EvCreat,d1 move.w #WAITINC,d2 move.w #SIGINC,d3 trap #0 dc.w FEvent bcs.w setuperr move.l d0,d7* moveq #0,d0 moveq #0,d1 moveq #1,d2 moveq #3,d3 moveq #0,d4 lea childpm(pc),a1 lea myname(pc),a0 trap #0 dc.w FFork bcs.w setuperr move.w d0,d4** Bounded, like every wait in fork.i: a child that never arrives must cost* this test its verdict, never the run. move.l #READYMAX,d3prdy lea rdymark(pc),a0 bsr ckmark bcc.s ppulse moveq #1,d0 bsr napticks subq.l #1,d3 bne.s prdy** Let the child reach its Ev$Wait, then pulse.ppulse move.l #RELDELAY,d0 bsr napticks moveq #0,d5 move.l d7,d0 move.w #EvPulse,d1 move.l #PULSVAL,d2 trap #0 dc.w FEvent bcc.s pwdone* A refused pulse is remembered, not reported yet.  The child is blocked on* an event that will now never be signalled, and leaving it that way would* outlive this test and wedge the rest of the run, so the reap below has to* happen either way. move.w d1,d5*pwdone move.l #DONEMAX,d3pwloop lea dnmark(pc),a0 bsr ckmark bcc.s preap moveq #1,d0 bsr napticks subq.l #1,d3 bne.s pwloop** Never came back.  Signal 0 is the one the manual guarantees: "This signal* terminates the receiving process, regardless of the state of its signal* mask, and is not intercepted by the intercept handler." moveq #0,d0 move.w d4,d0 moveq #0,d1 trap #0 dc.w FSend moveq #20,d3phwait trap #0 dc.w FWait bcs.s phung cmp.w d4,d0 beq.s phung subq.w #1,d3 bne.s phwaitphung move.l #HUNG,d6 bra.s pverd** Bounded, because F$Wait is documented to return early on a signal with* "d0.w contains zero, since no child process has terminated" (page 1-71).preap moveq #20,d3pwait trap #0 dc.w FWait bcs.w setuperr cmp.w d4,d0 beq.s pgot subq.w #1,d3 bne.s pwait move.w #SPNOWAIT,d1 bra.w setuperr** Decode fork.i's bands: only the 1000 band is an observation.pgot moveq #0,d6 move.w d1,d6 cmpi.l #2000,d6 blt.s pobs sub.l #2000,d6 move.w d6,d1 bra.w setuperrpobs cmpi.l #1000,d6 blt.s pdied sub.l #1000,d6 bra.s pverdpdied move.w d6,d1 bra.w setuperr** A refused Ev$Pulse outranks whatever the child made of a pulse that never* happened: its error code is the observation, and refusing the call is the* failure this test exists for.pverd tst.w d5 beq.s pdelet moveq #0,d6 move.w d5,d6pdelet lea evname(pc),a0 move.w #EvDelet,d1 trap #0 dc.w FEvent cmpi.l #EXPECT,d6 beq.w ispass bra.w isfail** ---- child: block on the event, and report what woke it ----child lea evname(pc),a0 move.w #EvLink,d1 trap #0 dc.w FEvent bcs.w chfail move.l d0,d7* The event is linked and the range is settled; Ev$Wait is the very next* thing this process does, which is what chready promises the parent. bsr chready move.l d7,d0 move.w #EvWait,d1 move.l #PULSVAL,d2 move.l #PULSVAL,d3 trap #0 dc.w FEvent bcs.w chfail move.l d1,d6 bra.w chdone* use verdict.i use fork.i use report.i*evname dc.b "cf41ev",0myname dc.b "t41evwake",0idstr dc.b "RESULT t41 ",0passtr dc.b "PASS",0failstr dc.b "FAIL",0errstr dc.b "ERROR",0skipstr dc.b "SKIP",0obsstr dc.b "  obs=",0expstr dc.b " exp=",0descstr dc.b "  Ev$Pulse wakes a process already waiting on the event",0 ends